<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Cook</h1>
<p>Skill
Class: Ranger (guild level 10), Druid (guild level 18)
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>cook &lt;food&gt;
</pre>
<p>Builds a small campfire and cooks a piece of food on it: meat from 
butchering, a fish, a plant. Cooked food fills you more, and cooking burns 
away some of any poison in it; a weak poison is gone altogether. Food can 
be cooked only once.
</p><p>You need open ground for a fire: not in a city or indoors, and not on 
water. Your skill and your dexterity decide whether you find enough to 
start a fire, and some lands give less kindling than others. If a 
campfire is already burning, you cook on it without building another. You 
need some endurance left, and you can't cook while fighting.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Butcher</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Skin</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Eat</a>
</pre>




</div>